#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fddd54e-2f69-5317-9273-59acf0420171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266424} {:answer/id #uuid "488b4f03-ec81-5e5e-88ac-1e1b03de77fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266792} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2ad35c-a214-5c83-bfd9-e7a6a53c9023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267099} {:answer/id #uuid "c18a481a-15ba-5133-9b96-62027df826c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267872} {:answer/id #uuid "ff581e6d-531a-50a8-93f1-45b62be1bbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c18a481a-15ba-5133-9b96-62027df826c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267872} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2163251-a2b2-5338-af76-79765630ea17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2bb923d-a428-53a1-96e5-4cae59c3d2d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138064" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge -2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-2(1)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -2.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-2.$ But before we conclude that $-2$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4(0)^{2}-(0)^{2}-2(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum and Minimum Values of a Quadratic Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ad65d6-22ea-5a70-a6fc-c7a394b78979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503111} {:answer/id #uuid "84bc382e-bb1a-53e0-9616-39f48f878732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503253} {:answer/id #uuid "85e05f05-a7d1-5ce5-afb1-7cfe2bb20cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503254} {:answer/id #uuid "957979fc-282e-5501-883c-530bce9d9ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503275} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8a228b-4bc9-587e-9614-77df0af9703d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc8a228b-4bc9-587e-9614-77df0af9703d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503425} :answer-field/id #uuid "53d0c528-6bbe-5382-9d7c-bfcd745b246c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8706edb2-e78b-5b3f-a44f-7250c01b8006" :question/math-academy-id "q-138072" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,1,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum and Minimum Values of a Quadratic Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53998127-850c-52ba-bb5b-642fd8be09d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503142} {:answer/id #uuid "646349e3-b930-50b5-8fa8-ca955067823e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503176} {:answer/id #uuid "79f97822-f108-5494-a037-0fa3ba02771b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503230} {:answer/id #uuid "9947b2d7-78d2-510d-a31f-a38e1ffbf62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503286} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c637b0-037f-510d-bebd-8c09cb3851b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9947b2d7-78d2-510d-a31f-a38e1ffbf62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503286} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b28165-ff27-54aa-8d84-67be182b4e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5347ea8e-b936-5670-b92f-f003075bcc63" :question/math-academy-id "q-138073" :question/problem "Find the  maximum value of $Q(x)=-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,1,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48ff6dc6-4553-5e13-910b-8df5f5a3bb78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503117} {:answer/id #uuid "4b434ef3-0980-5783-ad7e-eefe4f77ca09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503121} {:answer/id #uuid "55b888f5-b538-5f15-a7af-99357234caef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 